    "https://ethz.ch/en/the-eth-zurich/working-teaching-and-research/faculty/faculty-affairs/ausgeschriebene-professuren/architektur-und-bauwissenschaften/Prof_Civic_Arch.html": {
      "title": "Professors of Civic Architecture",
      "description": "Professors of Civic Architecture | ETH Zurich Homepage Navigation Search Content Footer Contact Sitemap Header Main Navigation News & events ETH Zurich Studies at ETH Zurich Doctorate Research Industry & Knowledge Transfer Campus Search Search en EN DE FR (TA) IT (TA) Departments ETH Zurich Select a department Departments D-ARCH: Architecture D-BAUG: Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering D-BSSE: Biosystems Science and Engineering D-INFK: Computer Science D-ITET: Information Technology and Electrical Engineering D-MATL: Department of Materials D-MAVT: Mechanical and Process Engineering D-BIOL: Biology D-CHAB: Chemistry and Applied Biosciences D-MATH: Mathematics D-PHYS: Physics D-EAPS: Earth and Planetary Sciences D-HEST: Health Sciences and Technology D-USYS: Environmental Systems Science D-MTEC: Management, Technology and Economics D-GESS: Humanities, Social and Political Sciences Language Selection en English Deutsch Français (TA) Italiano (TA) You are here Homepage ETH Zurich … Working, teaching and research Portal for Professors Office for Faculty Affairs Open faculty positions Architektur und Bauwissenschaften Professors of Civic Architecture Professors of Civic Architecture The Department of Architecture ( www.arch.ethz.ch ) at ETH Zurich invites applications for two professorships in civic architecture, both based at the Institute of Design and Architecture IEA ( www.iea.arch.ethz.ch ). Inspired by the challenge of creating spaces for a variety of communities and collective practices in contemporary urban territories, these new professorships focus on the character and role of civic architecture. We invite candidates with diverse and distinct approaches spanning the wide spectrum of civic architecture, which may include an emphasis on more monumental or everyday buildings, and range from locally grounded to cross-cultural practices. Through the teaching of design studios and lectures in the Bachelor's and Master's degree programmes in Architecture, including the supervision of Master's theses, the new professors will explore the theoretical foundations, methodological skills and design approaches of civic buildings and urban spaces. Situated at the intersection of architecture, urban studies, social responsibility and sustainable development, they are expected to demonstrate deep knowledge of urban history, governance and legal frameworks, and to promote a contextual and sustainable vision of architecture that reflects on what brings citizens together. Contemporary digital design and production techniques are generally an integral part of the sustainable architecture debate. The new professors are expected to develop a cutting-edge research agenda focused on architectural projects that engage with society and on resilient and inclusive urban spaces. They should be interested in interdisciplinary collaboration within the Department of Architecture and across ETH, particularly with the Institute of Design and Architecture (IEA) and the Institute of Landscape and Urban Studies (LUS), as well as with public agencies and members of civil society. The successful candidates must have a substantial built oeuvre and competence in design and realization of high-quality architecture with civic relevance. Qualifications include a university degree, accreditation by architects and usually experience, both in research and teaching. Responsible leadership of a group and a contribution to the development of the Department of Architecture beyond the boundaries of the discipline are expected. Courses at ETH Zurich are generally taught in German or English. ETH Zurich is an equal opportunity and family-friendly employer, values diversity , and is responsive to the needs of dual-career couples . Please apply online Applications should include a covering letter; a curriculum vitae; a list of publications; three statements on a) research, b) teaching, c) leadership; a project portfolio; descriptions of the three most important achievements*; and a certificate of the highest degree. Please note that the covering letter should be formally addressed to the President of ETH Zurich, Prof. Dr. Joël Mesot. The closing date for applications is 31 August 2026. Further information about D-ARCH can be found on our website . Questions regarding the position should be primarily directed to faculty-recruiting@sl.ethz.ch (no applications). Please note that applications should be submitted through our online application tool (see link above). *ETH Zurich emphasizes qualitative assessment of academic accomplishments. This is why you are kindly asked to submit a short description of your three most important achievements (maximum a half page each; no more than two pages each in case of images). Besides research findings and buildings, these could also be extraordinary achievements in teaching and its further development, services in the benefit of the academic community or society, software development, patents, knowledge transfer and its practical application, spin-off companies or similar. Job-sharing applications are possible under certain conditions . However, each applicant should submit her/his own application, explicitly reference the job-sharing proposal in the cover letter, and add a jointly authored document explaining the vision for the shared professorship. Footer Recommended links Media information Search Keyword or person Follow us Services Student portal Alumni association Staffnet Contact Login Departments D-ARCH Architecture D-BAUG Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering D-BIOL Biology D-BSSE Biosystems Science and Engineering D-CHAB Chemistry and Applied Biosciences D-EAPS Earth and Planetary Sciences D-GESS Humanities, Social and Political Sciences D-HEST Health Sciences and Technology D-INFK Computer Science D-ITET Information Technology and Electrical Engineering D-MATH Mathematics D-MATL Department of Materials D-MAVT Mechanical and Process Engineering D-MTEC Management, Technology and Economics D-PHYS Physics D-USYS Environmental Systems Science Table of contents and legal Sitemap Imprint Accessibility Statement Disclaimer & Copyright Data protection © 2026 Eidgenössische\n                    Technische Hochschule Zürich JavaScript has been disabled in your browser Choose your options ETH Zurich uses cookies to optimise its website and make it more user friendly. Cookies also help us to target our communications and marketing measures better. If you click on “Accept all cookies”, you are consenting to cookies being saved on your device. You can change what you would like to accept or reject in the cookie settings at any time. More about our cookies Cookie Settings Reject all Cookies Accept all Cookies Cookie settings We use cookies on our website. Cookies are small text files that are stored on your computer for a set period of time when you visit an ETH page. Cookies help us to statistically measure your usage of our website and continuously improve our service for you. You can deactivate some or all cookies at any time by adjusting your browser settings or you can delete them manually. If cookies are deactivated, you may no longer be able to use all the features of our website. Moreover, we primarily use first-party cookies. We do not use cookies from third-party services, such as advertising networks or social media platforms, without your explicit consent. Below, you can choose which types of cookie you would like to save in your browser. More about our cookies (Privacy Policy) Your user ID: e91ad41d-be2c-412b-a3aa-9b9ca8244f9d This user ID is a unique identifier that is used to save and refer to your cookie settings. If you request a copy of your consent history from us, this ID will make it easier to provide you with your history. Allow all cookies Managing cookie preferences Strictly necessary cookies Always active The website requires these cookies in order to function and you cannot deactivate them on your system.