    "https://ethz.ch/en/the-eth-zurich/working-teaching-and-research/faculty/faculty-affairs/ausgeschriebene-professuren/systemorientierte-naturwissenschaften/professur-fuer-biosensing-for-prevention-and-rehabilitation.html": {
      "title": "Professor of Biosensing for Prevention and Rehabilitation",
      "description": "Professor of Biosensing for Prevention and Rehabilitation | ETH Zurich Homepage Navigation Search Content Footer Contact Sitemap Header Main Navigation News & events ETH Zurich Studies at ETH Zurich Doctorate Research Industry & Knowledge Transfer Campus Search Search en EN DE FR (TA) IT (TA) Departments ETH Zurich Select a department Departments D-ARCH: Architecture D-BAUG: Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering D-BSSE: Biosystems Science and Engineering D-INFK: Computer Science D-ITET: Information Technology and Electrical Engineering D-MATL: Department of Materials D-MAVT: Mechanical and Process Engineering D-BIOL: Biology D-CHAB: Chemistry and Applied Biosciences D-MATH: Mathematics D-PHYS: Physics D-EAPS: Earth and Planetary Sciences D-HEST: Health Sciences and Technology D-USYS: Environmental Systems Science D-MTEC: Management, Technology and Economics D-GESS: Humanities, Social and Political Sciences Language Selection en English Deutsch Français (TA) Italiano (TA) You are here Homepage ETH Zurich … Working, teaching and research Portal for Professors Office for Faculty Affairs Open faculty positions System-​oriented Natural Sciences Professor of Biosensing for Prevention and Rehabilitation Professor of Biosensing for Prevention and Rehabilitation The Department of Health Sciences and Technology ( www.hest.ethz.ch ) at ETH Zurich invites applications for the above-mentioned position. The focus of this new professorship will be on the development of new diagnostic and prognostic methods (biosensors, biomarker analytics, artificial intelligence), which are expected to be validated via their integration in clinical workflows. The new professor is expected to contribute to digital/personalized health by improving prevention and therapies in prehabilitation and rehabilitation: fields of application include, but are not limited to oncology, geriatrics, neurology, paraplegiology or surgery. The research aims to develop biological, chemical, molecular, optical, electrical or other sensing technologies for an early diagnosis of possible pre- and postoperative complications as well as for health monitoring purposes. The professorship shall contribute to topics such as telehealth systems for remote clinical services, wireless medical devices as decision support systems and advanced data analytics (digital twins and artificial intelligence). Ideal candidates have a background in engineering with a specialization in biomechatronics, biochemistry, biomaterials, biomolecular analytics, or biostatistics, allowing them to build bridges from basic research to clinical application involving different scales from the molecular to the human level. Expertise in the field of biomedical engineering, with an emphasis on measurement sciences like biosensing technologies, biochemical analysis, molecular diagnosis, advanced materials applied to biosensing, or advanced data science techniques, is considered an asset. The new professorship will be established at ETH Zurich with premises mainly at EMPA, St. Gallen, and in conjunction with the clinical research at the Kantonsspital St. Gallen to develop patient-specific diagnostic tools and build rapid clinical translation of the research results. The successful candidate will also oversee the translation of materials, technologies, protocols, and AI algorithms to the clinics and industrial partners. Therefore, experience in or a strong link to clinical medicine is desired for the position. The new professor is expected to contribute to teaching at the undergraduate level (in German or English) and at the graduate level (in English). Engagement in practical teaching in the form of focus projects or teaching labs is also anticipated. ETH Zurich is an equal opportunity and family-friendly employer, values diversity , and is responsive to the needs of dual-career couples . Please apply online Applications should include a covering letter; a curriculum vitae; a list of publications; three statements on a) research, b) teaching, c) leadership; descriptions of the three most important achievements*; and a certificate of the highest degree. Please note that the covering letter should be formally addressed to the President of ETH Zurich, Prof. Dr. Joël Mesot. The closing date for applications is 15 September 2026. Further information about D-HEST can be found on our website . Questions regarding the position should be primarily directed to faculty-recruiting@sl.ethz.ch (no applications). Please note that applications should be submitted through our online application tool (see link above). *ETH Zurich emphasizes qualitative assessment of academic accomplishments. This is why you are kindly asked to submit a short description of your three most important achievements (maximum a half page each). Besides research findings, these could also be extraordinary achievements in teaching and its further development, services in the benefit of the academic community or society, software development, patents, knowledge transfer and its practical application, spin-​​​​​off companies or similar. Related content Professor or Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) of Critical Mineral Resources Professor of Human Nutrition Biology Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) of Earth and Planetary Evolution System-​oriented Natural Sciences Footer Recommended links Media information Search Keyword or person Follow us Services Student portal Alumni association Staffnet Contact Login Departments D-ARCH Architecture D-BAUG Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering D-BIOL Biology D-BSSE Biosystems Science and Engineering D-CHAB Chemistry and Applied Biosciences D-EAPS Earth and Planetary Sciences D-GESS Humanities, Social and Political Sciences D-HEST Health Sciences and Technology D-INFK Computer Science D-ITET Information Technology and Electrical Engineering D-MATH Mathematics D-MATL Department of Materials D-MAVT Mechanical and Process Engineering D-MTEC Management, T