    "https://ethz.ch/en/the-eth-zurich/working-teaching-and-research/faculty/faculty-affairs/ausgeschriebene-professuren/systemorientierte-naturwissenschaften/professur-fuer-human-nutrition-biology.html": {
      "title": "Professor of Human Nutrition Biology",
      "description": "Professor of Human Nutrition Biology | ETH Zurich Homepage Navigation Search Content Footer Contact Sitemap Header Main Navigation News & events ETH Zurich Studies at ETH Zurich Doctorate Research Industry & Knowledge Transfer Campus Search Search en EN DE FR (TA) IT (TA) Departments ETH Zurich Select a department Departments D-ARCH: Architecture D-BAUG: Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering D-BSSE: Biosystems Science and Engineering D-INFK: Computer Science D-ITET: Information Technology and Electrical Engineering D-MATL: Department of Materials D-MAVT: Mechanical and Process Engineering D-BIOL: Biology D-CHAB: Chemistry and Applied Biosciences D-MATH: Mathematics D-PHYS: Physics D-EAPS: Earth and Planetary Sciences D-HEST: Health Sciences and Technology D-USYS: Environmental Systems Science D-MTEC: Management, Technology and Economics D-GESS: Humanities, Social and Political Sciences Language Selection en English Deutsch Français (TA) Italiano (TA) You are here Homepage ETH Zurich … Working, teaching and research Portal for Professors Office for Faculty Affairs Open faculty positions System-​oriented Natural Sciences Professor of Human Nutrition Biology Professor of Human Nutrition Biology The Department of Health Sciences and Technology ( www.hest.ethz.ch ) at ETH Zurich invites applications for the above-mentioned position at the Institute of Food, Nutrition and Health ( www.ifnh.ethz.ch ). The new professor is expected to advance nutrition-centered research on the molecular and cellular basis of how diet, nutrients, and dietary patterns influence human health and disease across the lifespan, including healthy aging. The successful candidate will develop an innovative and mechanistic research program in nutrition biology with translational relevance, leveraging ETH Zurich’s interdisciplinary environment and state-of-the-art analytical and technological capabilities. Research directions may include the molecular basis of diet-driven metabolic phenotypes, precision/personalized nutrition, nutrition–inflammation interfaces, and metabolism- and nutrition-based strategies supporting prevention and health maintenance. The candidate must have an outstanding research background and international standing in nutrition biology or related fields. Demonstrated strength in building collaborations, including with clinical and/or population partners where relevant, is expected. Successful candidates are expected to establish and lead a competitive research team within the interactive environment at ETH Zurich and to contribute to teaching in the Food Science and Nutrition program. In general, at ETH Zurich undergraduate level courses are taught in German or English and graduate level courses are taught in English. ETH Zurich is an equal opportunity and family-friendly employer, values diversity , and is responsive to the needs of dual-career couples . Please apply online Applications should include a covering letter; a curriculum vitae; a list of publications; three statements on a) research, b) teaching, c) leadership; descriptions of the three most important achievements*; and a certificate of the highest degree. Please note that the covering letter should be formally addressed to the President of ETH Zurich, Prof. Dr. Joël Mesot. The closing date for applications is 15 November 2026 . Further information about D-HEST can be found on our website . Questions regarding the position should be primarily directed to faculty-recruiting@sl.ethz.ch (no applications). Please note that applications should be submitted through our online application tool (see link above). *ETH Zurich emphasizes qualitative assessment of academic accomplishments. This is why you are kindly asked to submit a short description of your three most important achievements (maximum a half page each). Besides research findings, these could also be extraordinary achievements in teaching and its further development, services in the benefit of the academic community or society, software development, patents, knowledge transfer and its practical application, spin-​​​​​off companies or similar. Related content Professor of Biosensing for Prevention and Rehabilitation Professor or Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) of Critical Mineral Resources Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) of Earth and Planetary Evolution System-​oriented Natural Sciences Footer Recommended links Media information Search Keyword or person Follow us Services Student portal Alumni association Staffnet Contact Login Departments D-ARCH Architecture D-BAUG Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering D-BIOL Biology D-BSSE Biosystems Science and Engineering D-CHAB Chemistry and Applied Biosciences D-EAPS Earth and Planetary Sciences D-GESS Humanities, Social and Political Sciences D-HEST Health Sciences and Technology D-INFK Computer Science D-ITET Information Technology and Electrical Engineering D-MATH Mathematics D-MATL Department of Materials D-MAVT Mechanical and Process Engineering D-MTEC Management, Technology and Economics D-PHYS Physics D-USYS Environmental Systems Science Table of contents and legal Sitemap Imprint Accessibility Statement Disclaimer & Copyright Data protection © 2026 Eidgenössische\n                    Technische Hochschule Zürich JavaScript has been disabled in your browser Choose your options ETH Zurich uses cookies to optimise its website and make it more user friendly. Cookies also help us to target our communications and marketing measures better. If you click on “Accept all cookies”, you are consenting to cookies being saved on your device. You can change what you would like to accept or reject in the cookie settings at any time. More about our cookies Cookie Settings Reject all Cookies Accept all Cookies Cookie settings We use cookies on our website. Cookies are small text files that are stored on your computer for a set period of time when you visit an ETH page. Cookies help us to statistically measure your